From: ON-FireLOS
Subject: [PATCH] cpuset: let system_server sort apps into groups

Android moves every app into a different cpuset group whenever it
switches between foreground and background (top-app, foreground,
background). system_server does that by writing to the group's tasks
file - for processes with a different uid. cgroup v1 only allows that
for root or the same uid, unless the group offers an allow_attach hook.
cpuctl had it, cpuset did not: every one of these moves failed with
EACCES ("add_tid_to_cgroup failed"), background apps kept running on all
four cores, and the foreground app never got into top-app.

cpuset gets the same hook as cpuctl: whoever has CAP_SYS_NICE may.
Corresponds to Android Common "ANDROID: cpuset: Add allow_attach hook for cpusets
on android".
---
--- a/kernel/cpuset.c	2026-10-29 14:22:03.292071188 +0000
+++ b/kernel/cpuset.c	2026-10-29 14:22:03.299406045 +0000
@@ -2078,6 +2078,7 @@
 	.can_attach	= cpuset_can_attach,
 	.cancel_attach	= cpuset_cancel_attach,
 	.attach		= cpuset_attach,
+	.allow_attach	= subsys_cgroup_allow_attach,
 	.bind		= cpuset_bind,
 	.fork		= cpuset_fork,
 	.legacy_cftypes	= files,
